<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adygea</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Republic of Adygea</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adygea is a republic of the Russian Federation in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a>, surrounded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krasnodar">Krasnodar</a> Krai, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maykop">Maykop</a>. It was created in 1922 as an autonomous region for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/circassians">Adyghe</a>, the western Circassians, descendants of those who remained after the mass expulsions of the 1860s. The Adyghe literary language is based on the Temirgoy dialect.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adygea.jpg" alt="Adygea" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vyacheslav Argenberg · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Acheshbok,_%D0%AE%D0%B6%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B5_%D0%BE%D1%82%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%B8_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D1%8B_%D0%90%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%88%D0%B1%D0%BE%D0%BA,_%D0%B4%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BC%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B5_%D0%BF%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B5_%D1%83%D1%81%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%8F_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BD%D0%B5%D0%B3%D0%BE_%D0%BB%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%B0,_%D0%97%D0%B0%D0%BF%D0%B0%D0%B4%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B9_%D0%9A%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%BA%D0%B0%D0%B7.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
